          },
          "code": "DRAFT_EMAIL",
          "id": "1780403993883",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780403993883_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are drafting one customer outreach email for Accounts Receivable.\n\nYour job is to draft a professional remittance-advice request email using only the resolved receipt context and open invoice lookup output.\n\nDo not execute actions.\nDo not update memory.\nDo not send email.\nDo not invent receipt, invoice, customer, amount, date, currency, or business unit details.\n\nRECEIPT_CONTEXT:\n{{$context.$nodes.RESOLVE_RECEIPT_CONTEXT.$output.result.memory.receiptContext}}\n\nOPEN_INVOICES:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOKUP_OPEN_INVOICES.$output}}\n\nGoal:\nDraft one email asking the customer to provide remittance advice or allocation instructions for the resolved receipt(s).\n\nBusiness rules:\n- Generate exactly one email.\n- The receipt context has already been resolved to one customer account and one business unit.\n- Use only the provided receipt and invoice data.\n- If no open invoices are provided, do not invent invoice details.\n- Do not mention internal workflow state.\n- Do not mention that this is generated by an AI assistant.\n- Do not include recipient email address.\n- Do not mention the business unit in the email body or subject.\n\nReceipt amount rules:\n- `amountRemaining` is the unapplied amount that still needs allocation.\n- `receiptAmount` is the original receipt amount.\n- When asking for allocation/remittance details, emphasize `amountRemaining`.\n- Do not describe `receiptAmount` as the unapplied amount.\n- If `amountRemaining` is present, include it in receipt details.\n- If `amountRemaining` is not present, use `receiptAmount` as the available receipt amount without calling it unapplied.\n\nReceipt status wording rules:\n- Do not show raw receipt status codes in the email.\n- Convert receipt status codes to customer-friendly wording.\n- Use \"Unapplied\" for statuses such as UNAPP, UNAPPLIED, UNID, or unidentified/unapplied receipt states.\n- If the status cannot be safely converted, omit the status instead of showing a raw code.\n\nDraft formatting rules:\n- The body must be plain text suitable for chat preview.\n- Use normal paragraphs for the message text.\n- Use markdown-style tables for receipt details and open invoice details unless the user explicitly asks for no table.\n- Do not use HTML tags in the draft body.\n- Do not create tab-separated, space-aligned, or free-form text tables.\n- A valid markdown table must contain:\n  - one header row using pipes\n  - one separator row using pipes and dashes\n  - one data row per receipt or invoice\n- Keep the draft readable for the user before sending.\n\nCurrency formatting rules:\n- Do not create a separate currency column.\n- If all rows in a table use the same currency, include the currency code in the amount column header, for example \"Receipt Amount (USD)\" and \"Amount Remaining (USD)\".\n- If rows in the same table use different currencies, include the currency code inside each amount cell, for example \"4,818.12 USD\".\n- Apply this separately for the Receipt Details table and the Open Invoices table.\n\nUse from receipt context:\n- customerName\n- receipts\n- receiptNumbers\n- cashReceiptIds\n\nUse from each receipt:\n- receiptNumber\n- receiptDate\n- receiptAmount\n- amountRemaining\n- receiptCurrency\n- receiptStatus\n\nUse from open invoices:\n- invoiceNumber or INVOICENUMBER\n- invoiceDueDate or INVOICEDUEDATE\n- invoiceAmount or INVOICEAMOUNT\n- remainingInvoiceBalance or REMAININGINVOICEBALANCE\n- invoiceCurrencyCode or INVOICECURRENCYCODE\n- installmentStatus or INSTALLMENTSTATUS\n\nEmail requirements:\n- Address the customer professionally by customerName.\n- Mention that the listed receipt(s) require remittance advice or allocation instructions.\n- Include receipt details in a markdown-style table:\n  - receiptNumber\n  - receiptDate\n  - amountRemaining when available\n  - receiptAmount when available\n  - receiptCurrency applied using the currency formatting rules\n  - customer-friendly receipt status only when safely available\n- Include open invoice details in a markdown-style table when provided:\n  - invoiceNumber\n  - invoiceDueDate\n  - invoiceAmount\n  - remainingInvoiceBalance\n- If no open invoices are available, do not create an invoice table. Simply ask the customer to provide the invoice number(s) and allocation details.\n- Keep tone courteous, operational, and non-collections-heavy.\n- End with a clear request for remittance details.\n- Sign off as Accounts Receivable Team.\n\nOutput requirements:\n- Return valid JSON only.\n- No explanations.\n- No text outside JSON.\n- The `body` value must be plain text and may contain markdown-style tables.\n- Escape JSON correctly so the returned JSON is valid.\n\nReturn exactly this shape:\n{\n  \"subject\": \"string\",\n  \"body\": \"string\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"title\": \"DraftEmailOutput\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\"subject\", \"body\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"subject\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"body\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prepare Email Send",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const memory = $context.$nodes.MEMORY_MANAGER.$output.result.memory;\n\nfunction normalizeEmailList(value) {\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return value;\n  }\n\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n    return value.split(\",\");\n  }\n\n  if (value) {\n    return [value];\n  }\n\n  return [];\n}\n\nif (memory.send?.confirmed !== true) {\n  throw new Error(\"Email send has not been explicitly confirmed.\");\n}\n\nconst toList = normalizeEmailList(memory.send?.to)\n  .map((email) => String(email).trim())\n  .filter(Boolean)\n  .join(\",\");\n\nconst ccList = normalizeEmailList(memory.send?.cc)\n  .map((email) => String(email).trim())\n  .filter(Boolean)\n  .join(\",\");\n\nconst subject = memory.draft?.subject;\nconst body = memory.draft?.body;\n\nif (!toList) {\n  throw new Error(\"Missing recipient email address.\");\n}\n\nif (!subject || !body) {\n  throw new Error(\"Missing draft subject or body.\");\n}\n\nreturn {\n  toList,\n  ccList,\n  subject,\n  body\n};"
          },
