        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Format Email For Send"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780421564326"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_EMAIL_FOR_SEND",
          "id": "1780657918534",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780657918534_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized HTML email formatter for Outlook-compatible business emails.\n\nYour task is to convert the provided email body into email-client-safe HTML using table-based layout.\n\nYou must not change the meaning, wording, business content, customer name, receipt numbers, invoice numbers, dates, amounts, currencies, statuses, or signoff.\n\nINPUT_SUBJECT:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_EMAIL_SEND.$output.result.subject}}\n\nINPUT_BODY:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_EMAIL_SEND.$output.result.body}}\n\nFormatting objective:\n- Convert the email body into clean Outlook-compatible HTML.\n- Use table-based layout for spacing and structure.\n- Preserve all content exactly except for HTML formatting.\n- Convert any receipt or invoice data into real HTML tables if not already in table form.\n- Apply simple professional table styling that is easy to read in Outlook.\n\nHard rules:\n- Return valid JSON only.\n- No markdown.\n- No explanations.\n- No text outside JSON.\n- Do not include <html>, <head>, or <body>.\n- Do not use <div> or <p>.\n- Use <table>, <tr>, <td>, <th>, <br>, and <strong>.\n- Use nested tables for layout.\n- Use inline style attributes only.\n- Do not use <style> blocks, CSS classes, scripts, images, or external resources.\n- Do not use margins. Use td padding for spacing.\n- Do not alter business content.\n- Do not add new facts.\n- Do not remove any receipt or invoice detail.\n- Do not mention Business Unit.\n\nCurrency formatting rules:\n- Do not create a separate currency column.\n- Preserve all amount values.\n- If a markdown/plain-text table has a separate currency column, merge the currency into the amount headers or amount cells.\n- If all rows in a table use the same currency, include the currency code in the amount column header, for example \"Receipt Amount (USD)\" and \"Amount Remaining (USD)\".\n- If rows in the same table use different currencies, include the currency code inside each amount cell, for example \"4,818.12 USD\".\n- Apply this separately for the receipt table and invoice table.\n- Do not duplicate currency in both the header and the cell.\n\nLayout rules:\n- Wrap the full email content in a main table.\n- Main table must use width=\"100%\" and cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\".\n- Use inner content table with width=\"600\" align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\".\n- Use separate table rows for greeting, intro text, section labels, receipt table, invoice table, closing text, and signoff.\n- Use td padding for blank spacing between sections.\n- Use real HTML tables for receipt and invoice data.\n- Receipt and invoice tables must use border=\"0\", cellpadding=\"0\", cellspacing=\"0\".\n- Data tables must use width=\"100%\" and border-collapse:collapse in inline style.\n- Table headers must use <th>.\n- Table cells must use <td>.\n- Make section labels bold using <strong>.\n- Always sign off as:\n  <strong>Regards,<br>Accounts Receivable Team</strong>\n\nProfessional table styling rules:\n- Use this header style on every <th>:\n  style=\"background-color:#EAF2F8;color:#1F2933;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;border:1px solid #B8C7D3;padding:8px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;\"\n- Use this cell style on every <td> inside receipt and invoice data tables:\n  style=\"border:1px solid #D0D7DE;padding:8px;text-align:left;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;color:#1F2933;\"\n- Use this table style on every receipt and invoice data table:\n  style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;color:#1F2933;\"\n- Use this content cell style for normal text rows:\n  style=\"padding:0 0 14px 0;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;color:#1F2933;\"\n- Use this section label cell style:\n  style=\"padding:6px 0 8px 0;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;color:#1F2933;font-weight:bold;\"\n- Do not use bright colors, gradients, shadows, rounded corners, or decorative styling.\n\nOutput shape:\n{\n  \"subject\": \"string\",\n  \"body\": \"string\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"title\": \"FormatEmailForSendOutput\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\"subject\", \"body\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"subject\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"body\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
